            If you only occasionally need to grind or cut concrete, a 4-1/2-inch grinder with a diamond cup wheel or blade handles small jobs. Large floor-grinding projects need dedicated equipment, and our guide to <a href="/acid-etching-vs-grinding-garage-floor/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">acid etching vs grinding a garage floor</a> explains when grinding is worth it.
          </p>
